@pickxd2035 The direct ancestors of the Indo-Europeans did not originate directly in Siberia as a distinct linguistic or cultural group, though their genetic lineage traces a deep historical link back to ancient Siberian-related populations.

Genetic Roots vs. Linguistic Origin
• Ancient North Eurasian (ANE) Ancestry: Genetic studies show that the people of the Yamnaya culture—widely considered the main vectors of the Proto-Indo-European language family—derived a significant portion of their ancestry from Eastern Hunter-Gatherers (EHGs). These EHGs, in turn, inherited ancestry from the Ancient North Eurasians (ANEs), a deep ancestral population represented by the 24,000-year-old Mal'ta boy from southern Siberia.
